## 7. Seed Demo Film

Create or ingest one original 45–90 second short mystery film.

Suggested narrative:

> A traveller enters a hotel room, sees an unfamiliar city outside, finds a newspaper carrying a warning, and notices a television bulletin that reveals the next clue.

The film must contain three clean edit boundaries.

### Slot 1: City Establishing Shot

Duration: 3–6 seconds

Narrative purpose:

- establish where the story is taking place.

Personalizable:

- city;
- weather;
- signage language;
- ambient environment.

Immutable:

- time of day;
- camera direction;
- emotional tone;
- duration range.

Preferred generation method:

1. Nano Banana generates a keyframe.
2. Omni animates the keyframe.

Fallback:

- canonical generic city clip.

### Slot 2: Newspaper or Phone Clue

Duration: 3–5 seconds

Narrative purpose:

- reveal that the antagonist has returned.

Personalizable:

- language;
- city;
- publication name;
- typography;
- local date format.

Immutable:

- antagonist name;
- plot fact;
- warning symbol;
- clue meaning.

Preferred generation method:

1. Nano Banana creates the localized prop.
2. Either:
   - traditional compositing into a prepared plate; or
   - Omni creates a short close-up animation.

Fallback:

- canonical English clue.

### Slot 3: TV Bulletin or Billboard

Duration: 3–6 seconds

Narrative purpose:

- provide a final contextual clue.

Personalizable:

- language;
- location;
- broadcast graphics;
- optional sponsor category.

Immutable:

- story fact;
- character reaction timing;
- required visual symbol.

Preferred generation method:

1. Nano Banana creates broadcast graphic.
2. Omni animates or embeds it into the scene.

Fallback:

- canonical generic bulletin.

