## 18. Viewer Experience UI

### Profile selector

Cards for three seeded profiles.

Each card displays:

- name;
- city;
- language;
- compact flag or location icon;
- “Watch this cut” CTA.

Also include:

- “Create custom profile” CTA.

### Preparation screen

Show:

- selected profile;
- movie poster;
- three slot statuses.

Example:

```text
Preparing your cut

✓ City reveal — cached
✓ Newspaper clue — cached
◌ TV bulletin — generating

You can start watching now.
Canonical footage will be used if a personalized segment is not ready.
```

The main CTA must remain enabled.

### Player HUD

Keep technical detail subtle.

Visible:

- movie title;
- profile name;
- progress bar;
- three adaptive slot markers.

Optional debug mode:

- cache hit;
- model name;
- job status;
- active asset URL;
- fallback state.

---

## 19. Compare Screen

Display three cuts side by side.

### Required behavior

- synchronized play/pause;
- synchronized seek;
- jump to slot;
- mute all but selected player;
- profile labels;
- show current slot metadata;
- canonical toggle.

Recommended layout:

```text
┌──────────────────┬──────────────────┬──────────────────┐
│ Visakhapatnam    │ Tokyo            │ San Francisco    │
│ Telugu           │ Japanese         │ English          │
│ [video]          │ [video]          │ [video]          │
└──────────────────┴──────────────────┴──────────────────┘

[Play all] [Pause] [City slot] [Clue slot] [TV slot]
```

For performance, comparison may use pre-rendered complete cuts rather than three segmented players.

---

## 20. Live Demo Strategy

Use a hybrid approach.

### Pre-generated

Pre-generate and approve:

- all three slots for Visakhapatnam/Telugu;
- all three slots for Tokyo/Japanese;
- all three slots for San Francisco/English;
- all canonical fallback clips;
- complete comparison cuts.

### Generate live

Create a fourth profile:

```json
{
  "displayName": "Camille",
  "city": "Paris",
  "country": "France",
  "locale": "fr-FR",
  "languageLabel": "French"
}
```

Generate only one bounded slot live.

Preferred order:

1. Nano Banana generates a newspaper, TV graphic, or city keyframe.
2. Show the generated still immediately.
3. Start Omni animation.
4. Continue showing cached profiles and architecture.
5. When Omni completes, preview the animated insert.
6. If Omni fails or finishes late, demonstrate canonical fallback.

### Important rule

The main demo must never depend on the live generation succeeding.

The live generation is a bonus proof of dynamism.

---

## 21. Demo Sequence

Target length: 4–6 minutes.

### Step 1 — Canonical film

Play 20–30 seconds of the canonical version.

Narration:

> Every viewer normally receives this cut.

### Step 2 — Viewer profile

Select Visakhapatnam/Telugu.

Narration:

> This viewer has explicitly chosen a city and language.

### Step 3 — Personalized playback

Play the personalized cut.

Highlight:

- city shot;
- Telugu clue;
- localized TV graphic.

### Step 4 — Director control

Open Director Studio.

Show:

- only three slots can change;
- immutable narrative facts;
- fallback clip;
- approved variants.

### Step 5 — Comparison

Open the compare screen.

Play the three versions side by side.

Narration:

> The story remains identical. Only director-approved surfaces adapt.

### Step 6 — Live generation

Add Paris/French profile.

Generate one slot.

### Step 7 — Fallback

Use a demo toggle to simulate a failed or late generation.

Show:

```text
Generation deadline exceeded.
Using director-approved canonical segment.
```

### Step 8 — Closing

End with:

> One story. A different world for every viewer.

---

## 22. API Endpoints

### Movies

```text
GET    /api/movies
GET    /api/movies/:movieId
POST   /api/movies
PATCH  /api/movies/:movieId
```

### Slots

```text
GET    /api/movies/:movieId/slots
POST   /api/movies/:movieId/slots
PATCH  /api/slots/:slotId
```

### Profiles

```text
GET    /api/profiles
POST   /api/profiles
GET    /api/profiles/:profileId
```

### Cut preparation

```text
POST   /api/cuts/prepare
GET    /api/cuts/:movieId/:profileId
```

Request:

```json
{
  "movieId": "hotel-mystery-001",
  "profileId": "vizag-te"
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "movieId": "hotel-mystery-001",
  "profileId": "vizag-te",
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "canonical-01",
      "type": "CANONICAL",
      "activeUrl": "/media/canonical/part-01.mp4",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "id": "slot-city",
      "type": "ADAPTIVE",
      "activeUrl": "/media/generated/vizag-te/slot-city.mp4",
      "status": "READY",
      "source": "CACHE_HIT"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Generation

```text
POST   /api/generation/jobs
GET    /api/generation/jobs/:jobId
POST   /api/generation/jobs/:jobId/retry
POST   /api/generation/jobs/:jobId/cancel
```

### Approval

```text
POST   /api/assets/:assetId/approve
POST   /api/assets/:assetId/reject
```

### Demo controls

```text
POST   /api/demo/simulate-failure
POST   /api/demo/clear-cache
POST   /api/demo/seed
```

Demo-only endpoints must be disabled outside development/demo mode.

