## 23. Service Boundaries

Create these modules:

```text
src/
├── app/
├── components/
├── lib/
│   ├── ai/
│   │   ├── image-generation.service.ts
│   │   ├── video-generation.service.ts
│   │   ├── prompt-builder.ts
│   │   └── validation.service.ts
│   ├── cache/
│   │   ├── cache-key.ts
│   │   └── cache.repository.ts
│   ├── jobs/
│   │   ├── generation-queue.ts
│   │   └── generation-worker.ts
│   ├── media/
│   │   ├── media-storage.ts
│   │   ├── video-probe.ts
│   │   └── ffmpeg.ts
│   ├── playback/
│   │   ├── cut-resolver.ts
│   │   └── segment-scheduler.ts
│   ├── repositories/
│   └── types/
└── public/
    └── media/
```

Do not call Gemini models directly from UI components.

---

## 24. Mock Mode

The application must work even without live model access.

Environment variable:

```text
AI_MODE=mock | live
```

### Mock mode behavior

- returns seeded Nano Banana images;
- returns seeded Omni video clips;
- simulates latency;
- supports simulated failure;
- populates realistic job states;
- demonstrates cache hit and miss.

Suggested delays:

```text
Nano Banana: 1.5 seconds
Omni: 8–20 seconds
Validation: 1 second
```

### Live mode behavior

- performs real server-side API calls;
- stores raw response IDs;
- handles retries;
- records latency and errors;
- falls back safely.

---

## 25. Environment Variables

```bash
AI_MODE=mock

GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image
GEMINI_VIDEO_MODEL=gemini-omni-flash-preview

DATABASE_URL=
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=

MEDIA_STORAGE_DRIVER=local
MEDIA_STORAGE_BUCKET=

NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
ENABLE_DEMO_CONTROLS=true
```

Never expose `GEMINI_API_KEY` to the browser.

---

## 26. Error Handling

Every generation job must have:

- timeout;
- retry count;
- error code;
- human-readable failure reason;
- fallback asset;
- idempotency through cache key.

Suggested retry policy:

- image generation: 2 retries;
- video generation: 1 retry;
- validation: 1 retry;
- do not retry after playback deadline for the current session.

Failure states:

```ts
export type GenerationFailureCode =
  | "MODEL_TIMEOUT"
  | "MODEL_REJECTED"
  | "INVALID_OUTPUT"
  | "STORAGE_FAILURE"
  | "VALIDATION_FAILED"
  | "DEADLINE_EXCEEDED"
  | "UNKNOWN";
```

UI copy:

```text
Personalized version unavailable.
Playing the director-approved original.
```

---

## 27. Security and Privacy

- Profiles must use user-declared data only.
- Do not infer race, religion, politics, health, or socioeconomic status.
- Do not upload private user media in the demo.
- Do not use real news claims.
- Do not use a real person as a fictional criminal or suspect.
- Do not use celebrity footage.
- Do not imply actor endorsement of personalized products.
- Store only the minimum profile fields needed for generation.
- Add an option to delete ad hoc profiles and generated assets.
- Keep API keys server-side.
- Validate all uploaded media types and sizes.

---

## 28. Observability

Log:

- movie ID;
- slot ID;
- profile ID;
- cache key;
- cache hit/miss;
- model;
- generation start;
- generation completion;
- latency;
- validation result;
- fallback use;
- playback selection.

Add a small metrics panel:

```text
Cache hit rate
Average Nano Banana latency
Average Omni latency
Fallback rate
Validated asset count
Approved asset count
```

For the demo, local in-memory metrics are acceptable.

