## 29. Build Phases

### Phase 1 — Deterministic prototype

- Set up app.
- Seed movie, slots, and profiles.
- Build Director Studio static UI.
- Build profile selector.
- Build segmented player.
- Use pre-generated local assets.
- Build compare screen.
- Implement fallback behavior.

### Phase 2 — Job and cache system

- Add generation jobs.
- Add cache keys.
- Add job status UI.
- Add mock generation latency.
- Add simulated failure.
- Add approval flow.

### Phase 3 — Nano Banana integration

- Implement image generation service.
- Generate keyframes and props.
- Save outputs.
- Validate dimensions and metadata.
- Add director preview.

### Phase 4 — Omni integration

- Implement short video generation service.
- Support image-to-video.
- Save generated video.
- Validate duration and playback.
- Add retry and timeout handling.

### Phase 5 — Demo polish

- Pre-generate primary cuts.
- Render comparison videos.
- Add smooth player transitions.
- Add stage-friendly typography.
- Add demo reset button.
- Add debug panel.
- Test fallback repeatedly.
- Record backup screen capture.

---

## 30. Acceptance Criteria

### Director Studio

- [ ] One movie is visible.
- [ ] Exactly three adaptive slots appear on the timeline.
- [ ] Each slot exposes editable and immutable fields.
- [ ] Each slot has a canonical fallback.
- [ ] Generated variants can be previewed.
- [ ] Assets can be approved or rejected.

### Viewer flow

- [ ] Three seeded profiles appear.
- [ ] A custom profile can be created.
- [ ] Selecting a profile prepares a cut.
- [ ] Playback starts without waiting for generation.
- [ ] Cached personalized clips play when available.
- [ ] Fallback clips play when needed.
- [ ] Slot status is visible.

### AI pipeline

- [ ] Nano Banana service can generate or mock an image.
- [ ] Omni service can generate or mock a short video.
- [ ] Output is stored.
- [ ] Output is validated.
- [ ] Valid output is cached.
- [ ] Failed output never blocks playback.

### Compare screen

- [ ] Three profiles can be compared.
- [ ] Players can be synchronized.
- [ ] Viewer labels are visible.
- [ ] Users can jump to each adaptive slot.

### Demo reliability

- [ ] Primary cuts are pre-generated.
- [ ] Demo works with AI APIs disabled.
- [ ] Live generation is optional.
- [ ] Failure can be simulated.
- [ ] Canonical fallback works every time.
- [ ] Demo can be reset in one click.

---

## 31. Suggested Visual Design

Use a cinematic but restrained interface.

### Visual language

- dark background;
- warm white text;
- film-strip inspired timeline;
- violet or indigo accent for adaptive slots;
- green for ready;
- amber for generating;
- gray for fallback;
- red only for failed jobs.

### Typography

Use:

- Inter, Geist, or similar for UI;
- optional serif display font for movie title.

### Motion

- subtle timeline pulse while generating;
- gentle fade when switching segments;
- no excessive animation;
- no sci-fi hologram aesthetic unless it supports clarity.

---

